          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 7 | Part-II"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.087,
            0.847,
            0.147
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "? For the weighing scale problems in figures 7.6, 7.7, 7.8, 7.9, 7.10, and 7.11, frame equations by using letter-numbers to denote the unknown weight."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.15,
            0.846,
            0.172
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "For the problem in Fig. 7.6, let us denote the weight of one fried egg as e."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.175,
            0.846,
            0.215
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Since each slice of bread is 2, we have "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "2+2+2=6"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " on one side and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "e + e"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " on the other side. Since they are equal, we have"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.442,
            0.215,
            0.557,
            0.232
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_4_equation_4.jpg",
          "content": "6 = e + e,  or"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.465,
            0.238,
            0.534,
            0.255
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_4_equation_5.jpg",
          "content": "2 e = 6 ."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.261,
            0.847,
            0.32
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "For the problem in Fig. "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "7.7, 凳  = 4,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , and we can denote the weight of one as y. So, we have 16 on one side, and 4 + 2y on the other side. Thus, we have the equation"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.442,
            0.325,
            0.555,
            0.344
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_4_equation_7.jpg",
          "content": "4+2y=16."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.353,
            0.846,
            0.395
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ Solve the equations that you frame and check if you get the same value for the unknown weight as you got previously."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.408,
            0.619,
            0.431
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Frame 5 equations. Find methods to solve them."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.818,
            0.386,
            0.904,
            0.437
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 10,
              "bbox": [
                0.818,
                0.386,
                0.904,
                0.437
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_4_image_10.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.459,
            0.656,
            0.485
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "7.2 Solving Equations Systematically"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.493,
            0.847,
            0.572
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "How did you solve the various equations framed in the previous section? One way to solve an equation is to substitute different values in place of the letter−number and to check which value makes LHS = RHS. For example, consider the equation 2n + 1 = 99."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.575,
            0.846,
            0.613
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "If we substitute n = 5, we get "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm{LHS} = \\underline{2} \\times (5) + 1 = 11"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . It is far away from 99, the RHS."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.191,
            0.613,
            0.745,
            0.633
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We can try n = 10. The LHS is 21. It is still not equal to 99."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.191,
            0.633,
            0.805,
            0.652
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Can we try n = 30? The LHS is now 61, still much lower than 99."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.191,
            0.652,
            0.762,
            0.67
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Let us try n = 40. The LHS is 81. We are getting closer to 99."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.191,
            0.671,
            0.715,
            0.69
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "When n = 50, the LHS is 101. This is just a bit too high."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.191,
            0.69,
            0.461,
            0.708
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "When n = 49, the LHS is 99!"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.191,
            0.709,
            0.764,
            0.728
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Therefore, the solution to the equation "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "2n + 1 = 99"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is n = 49."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.738,
            0.572,
            0.76
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Can this equation have any other solution?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 21,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.763,
            0.638,
            0.783
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "This method is called the "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "trial and error",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " method."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 22,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.787,
            0.597,
            0.807
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The trial and error method can be inefficient."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 23,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.821,
            0.565,
            0.845
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Try solving "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "5 x - 4 = 7"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " using trial and error."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 24,
          "bbox": [
            0.156,
            0.933,
            0.193,
            0.95
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "168"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
